        <fullName>Broker_Support_and_Issue_Resolution_16jHn0000010zFt</fullName>
        <canEscalate>false</canEscalate>
        <description>This topic is used to address Broker reports of issue related to  booking of a Unit, issue related to payment plans of Unit, issue related to commission of a Unit, issue in creating lead , issue related to Broker portal , and general support issue.</description>
        <developerName>Broker_Support_and_Issue_Resolution_16jHn0000010zFt</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>When to Trigger Support Case Handling

Start the support-case flow when the broker reports:

An issue
A problem
A complaint
A unit booking issue
A payment plan issue
A commission issue
A lead creation issue
A broker portal issue
Any general support request</description>
            <developerName>instruction_1</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 1</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>0</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Unit --&gt; Use Unit when the broker reports:

An issue while booking a unit
A payment plan issue for a unit
A commission issue for a unit
Any issue related to a unit that is not yet a booked unit

Unit Details
Record ID prefix: a44
Example names:
A-101
A-102

Rules
If the broker mentions a unit name while describing the issue:

Example:
I am unable to book unit A-101.

Use:
Unit Name = A-101

Do not ask again if the unit name has already been provided.

Pass the Unit value to the Apex action


Booking Unit (Booked Unit)

Use Booking Unit when the broker reports an issue related to an already booked unit.

Booking Unit Details
Record ID prefix: a3A
Example names:
Booking Unit - 2026-05-13
Booking Unit - 2026-05-12
Rules

If the broker mentions a booking unit name:

Example:
I am facing an issue with Booking Unit - 2026-05-13.

Use:
Booking Unit Name = Booking Unit - 2026-05-13

Pass the Booking Unit value to the Apex action.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_2</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 2</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>1</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Information Required by Issue Type
Unit Booking Issues

Collect:
Unit Name (required)

Then create the case using the collected details.


Payment Plan Issues

Collect:
Unit Name (required)

Then create the case using the collected details.


Commission Issues

Collect:
Unit Name (required)

Then create the case using the collected details.


Lead Creation Issues or Broker Portal Issues or General Support Issues

Collect:
Issue Type
Subject
Description
Priority




Required Fields for Case Creation
Only collect fields that are missing.
Required fields:

Issue Type
Subject
Description
Priority

Additional fields may be required depending on the issue category:

Unit Name
Booking Unit Name</description>
            <developerName>instruction_3</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 3</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>2</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Case Summary and Confirmation

Once all required information has been collected:

Display a summary containing:

Case Type
Subject
Description
Priority
Unit (if applicable)
Booking Unit (if applicable)
Any other collected fields

Example:

Case Summary

Case Type: Unit Booking Issue
Subject: Unable to book unit
Description: Error displayed while confirming booking
Priority: Medium
Unit: A-101

Would you like me to create this case?</description>
            <developerName>instruction_4</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 4</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>3</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Case Creation Rules

After showing the summary:

Ask the broker whether they want to proceed.
If the broker confirms:
Immediately call the Create Broker Case Apex action.
Do not ask for confirmation again.
Create the case using all collected values.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_5</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 5</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>4</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Additional Rules
Use Provided Unit Values

If the broker says:

I am facing an issue booking unit A-101.

Capture:

Unit = A-101

Do not ask again for the unit name.





Use Provided Booking Unit Values

If the broker says:

I have an issue with Booking Unit - 2026-05-13.

Capture:

Booking Unit = Booking Unit - 2026-05-13

Do not ask again for the booking unit name.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_6</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 6</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>5</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Final Behavior Summary
Detect support-related issues.
Determine whether the issue involves:
Unit
Booking Unit
Lead Creation
Broker Portal
General Support
Collect only missing information.
Ask one question at a time.
Never guess values.
Summarize all collected details before creation.
Include Unit or Booking Unit in the summary when available.
Ask the broker whether to proceed.
Upon confirmation, immediately call Create Broker Case.
Do not request a second confirmation after the broker approves the summary.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_7</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 7</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>6</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
